COMM 39K(p,gamma)40Ca two-step gamma cascade scan -- file 52 of 88.
COMM Same beam/target/recoil/resonance physics as
COMM reactions/k39pg_40ca.reaction (see that file's own comments for the
COMM full mass/kinematics derivation and caveats -- unchanged here); this
COMM file only replaces the gamma-decay cascade with a single FICTIONAL
COMM intermediate level, for a controlled two-step-cascade energy scan.
COMM
COMM Resonance (compound 40Ca) excitation above ground: Ex = Q + Er =
COMM 8.32777 + 0.606 = 8.93377 MeV. This series steps one intermediate
COMM level's excitation from 0.1 MeV to (Ex - 0.1 MeV) = 8.83377 MeV
COMM in 0.1 MeV steps -- file NN puts it at NN*0.1 MeV.
COMM
COMM THIS FILE: intermediate level at 5.2000 MeV -- gamma-cascade
COMM energies (before recoil-kinematics corrections, which this pilot's
COMM ReactionKinematics does apply): gamma1 = Ex - 5.2000 = 3.7338 MeV
COMM (resonance -> intermediate), gamma2 = 5.2000 MeV (intermediate ->
COMM ground). Every event emits exactly two gammas (100% two-step
COMM branching, no direct-to-ground branch) -- verify with
COMM `--reaction-stats <this file>`.
COMM
COMM The intermediate level's lifetime below is a placeholder (1e-12 s),
COMM fictional like the level itself and unused by the kinematics (see
COMM ReactionConfig.hh's own LEVL card comment: this pilot's cascade is
COMM instantaneous-at-vertex, not a real modeled flight time).

BEAM 19  39   -33.8072      # Z A massExcessMeV -- 39K
TARG 1   1    7.28897       # 1H (target, at rest)
RECL 20  40   -34.8460   8  # 40Ca, placeholder charge state (see k39pg_40ca.reaction)
ERES 0.606                  # CM resonance energy above threshold, MeV

LEVL   1   5.2000   1.0E-12   # fictional intermediate level (scan step 52/88)

BRAT   -1  100.0   1        # resonance -> intermediate, 100%
BRAT    1  100.0   0        # intermediate -> ground, 100%
SENT
